  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Does the command byte A of the music data. $c0-$cf set the note length. $f0-$f9 go through the handler table at $a08d."},
    {"at":6,"placement":"side","text":"Note length = entry (low nibble) of the duration table at $a03b."},
    {"at":32,"placement":"line","text":"Finds the command byte in the table at $a083. Y = 1 points to the argument."},
    {"at":61,"placement":"side","text":"No handler: the byte is not used."},
    {"at":62,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f0: rest. Waits for one note length without a new gate."},
    {"at":62,"placement":"side","text":"Stops the read of the voice for this tick."},
    {"at":86,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f1: sets the read offset of the voice to 0 and clears the gate. The tune starts again."},
    {"at":107,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f2: ends the tune of the voice. Stops the voice, its effects and the filter sweep."},
    {"at":124,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f3 n: loads instrument n, 12 bytes at $a384 + n * 12. Sets ADSR, waveform, pulse width and the effect steps."},
    {"at":132,"placement":"side","text":"Multiplies n by 12."},
    {"at":174,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 0: attack/decay. Byte 1: sustain/release."},
    {"at":186,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 2: waveform (high nibble) and pulse width high (low nibble)."},
    {"at":194,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 3: pulse width low. The pulse width bytes are inverted."},
    {"at":212,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 4: effect speed. Byte 5: effect flags."},
    {"at":226,"placement":"side","text":"Bytes 6-11: value and length of the 3 effect phases."},
    {"at":271,"placement":"side","text":"Flag bit 1: sets the sync bit."},
    {"at":287,"placement":"side","text":"Flag bit 2: sets triangle with ring modulation ($14)."},
    {"at":302,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f4 a b: note length = duration a + duration b (low nibbles, table at $a03b)."},
    {"at":349,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f5 n: the voice continues with tune n from its start. Clears the filter routing bit of the voice."},
    {"at":358,"placement":"side","text":"Clears the resonance and the filter bit of the voice."},
    {"at":378,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f6 n: sets CIA 1 timer B (the music tick rate) to entry n of the tempo table at $a05b."},
    {"at":402,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f7 n: plays tune n on the voice, then returns after this command (see cmd_return)."},
    {"at":419,"placement":"side","text":"Returns with X = music_voice * 2."},
    {"at":443,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f8: returns to the tune and read offset that cmd_call_tune saved."},
    {"at":466,"placement":"line","text":"Command $f9 n: loads filter setting n (11 bytes, pointer table at $a0a1) and starts the filter on this voice."},
    {"at":480,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 0: sweep speed. Bytes 1-2: start cutoff (high, low)."},
    {"at":497,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 3: resonance and routing, with the bit of this voice."},
    {"at":507,"placement":"side","text":"Byte 4: filter mode. Clears the voice 3 off bit."},
    {"at":519,"placement":"line","text":"Bytes 5-10: step (times 8) and length of the 3 sweep phases."}
  ],
